WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.173
This one is for the night your schedule moved.

00:00:03.123 --> 00:00:14.888
A flight, a shift change, a late event, a clock that went forward, or one weekend where you got up three hours later than usual and paid for it on Sunday.

00:00:14.888 --> 00:00:19.667
If that is the night you are having, you are not fighting insomnia right now.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:25.461
You are fighting a clock that is still set to the old time, and clocks move slowly.

00:00:25.461 --> 00:00:31.638
Roughly an hour a day, and less than that when you are being pushed later than your body prefers.

00:00:31.638 --> 00:00:36.917
That is worth knowing at three in the morning, because it changes what a win is.

00:00:36.917 --> 00:00:39.197
Tonight is not fixable.

00:00:39.197 --> 00:00:41.123
The next three days are.

00:00:41.123 --> 00:00:43.520
So tonight, keep it small.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:50.505
Do not lie in bed doing arithmetic about the time back home or the hours left before the alarm.

00:00:50.505 --> 00:00:54.491
Whatever the number is, it does not change the instruction.

00:00:54.491 --> 00:01:01.255
Let your jaw come apart, drop your shoulders, and let the out breath run longer than the in breath.

00:01:01.255 --> 00:01:02.932
Nothing to count.

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:27.704
If you are heavy, stay where you are and let the night do what it does.

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:31.521
If you are wired after twenty minutes or so, get up.

00:01:31.521 --> 00:01:38.110
Low light, chair, something boring, back to bed when your eyes are closing on their own.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:40.507
Same protocol, new cause.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:16.248
Now the part that actually moves a clock, and it is not what happens at night.

00:02:16.198 --> 00:02:18.977
It is light and it is your wake time.

00:02:18.977 --> 00:02:26.242
Pick the wake time you want to live on, the one that belongs to where you are now or to the schedule you are moving into.

00:02:26.242 --> 00:02:31.433
Set it, and hold it for three days, including the day you feel wrecked.

00:02:31.433 --> 00:02:35.315
That is the anchor, and everything else is negotiable.

00:02:35.315 --> 00:02:37.624
Then use light on purpose.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:44.551
If you need to wake up earlier than your body wants, get bright light into your eyes as soon as you get up.

00:02:44.551 --> 00:02:49.227
Outside, ten to twenty minutes, even under cloud.

00:02:49.227 --> 00:02:55.874
And keep the evening dim, low lamps, screens down, nothing bright in the last hour.

00:02:55.874 --> 00:02:58.859
If you need to move later, do the opposite.

00:02:58.859 --> 00:03:06.080
Keep the morning dim for the first hour and get bright light in the late afternoon and early evening.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.448
That is the whole mechanism.

00:03:08.448 --> 00:03:11.418
Light in the morning pulls you earlier.

00:03:11.418 --> 00:03:13.786
Light at night pushes you later.

00:03:13.786 --> 00:03:15.889
Everything else is detail.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:34.368
Two more things, and then I will leave you to the night.

00:03:34.318 --> 00:03:35.465
Naps.

00:03:35.465 --> 00:03:46.333
On a moved schedule, a nap is allowed, but twenty minutes, before three in the afternoon, and never as a substitute for holding the wake time.

00:03:46.333 --> 00:03:48.333
And expectations.

00:03:48.333 --> 00:03:52.833
Give it one day per hour of shift before you judge how it is going.

00:03:52.833 --> 00:03:59.818
If you flew across four hours, you are looking at about four days, and the fourth is usually fine.

00:03:59.818 --> 00:04:07.598
Judging it tomorrow is how people conclude the method broke when what actually happened is that they changed time zones.

00:04:07.598 --> 00:04:10.318
Tonight, nothing is required.

00:04:10.318 --> 00:04:14.495
Your clock is moving already, whether or not you sleep.

00:04:14.495 --> 00:04:17.421
Close your eyes and let it move.
